1
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:05,671
[GREMLINS CHITTERING ON TV]

2
00:00:06,256 --> 00:00:08,716
(Sheldon:)This movie baffles me
every time we watch it.

3
00:00:08,883 --> 00:00:10,173
(Leonard:)What do you mean?

4
00:00:10,343 --> 00:00:14,053
(Sheldon:)The instructions are very clear.
Don't feed the gremlins after midnight.

5
00:00:15,765 --> 00:00:18,435
(Sheldon:)Don't get the gremlins wet.

6
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:22,311
(Sheldon:)How hard is that?

7
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:24,776
(Penny(arriving):)Hi, guys.

8
00:00:24,941 --> 00:00:26,021
(Penny(arriving):)-Hi, honey.
-Hey.

9
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:28,612
Oh, we're "honey" now, are we?

10
00:00:28,778 --> 00:00:31,158
(Sheldon:)Yes. Since their relationship
became carnal...

11
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:33,992
(Sheldon:)...Penny has upgraded
his designated term of endearment...

12
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:36,699
(Sheldon:)...distinguishing him
from those she calls "sweetie"...

13
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:40,120
(Sheldon:)...in an attempt to soften
a thinly veiled insult.

14
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:43,503
(Penny:)You're boring people, sweetie.

15
00:00:44,085 --> 00:00:47,505
(Sheldon:)Although sometimes
she omits the veil entirely.

16
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:51,049
(Penny:)-So, what are you guys doing?
-Celebrating Columbus Day.

17
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:54,557
(Leonard:)We're watching Goonies, Gremlins
and Young Sherlock Holmes.

18
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,101
They're all written by Chris Columbus.

19
00:00:58,391 --> 00:01:01,101
(Penny:)Okay. What do you watch
on Thanksgiving?

